special_abilities:
  - name: "Familiarity with Sovietski Cybernetics"
    description: "Knows the bionics of the Sovietski and most Warlords of Russia well, and those of the NGR less so; can strip and rebuild a Light or Heavy Machine in hours. Working on Sovietski or Warlord cybernetics, bionics and their weapons: +10% to the skill roll and half the usual time. Working on Triax, Poland/Mindwerks, Coalition or other foreign technology: -10% and 25% longer. Not added to the sheet."
  - name: "Install Cybernetics and Bionics"
    description: "Installs and removes implants and bionics even under fire or in poor conditions; implants are quick and usually carry no penalty, bionics take longer. Cumulative penalties: -5% on an open battlefield or in the back of a truck, -5% more with poor tools, -5% more aboard a moving vehicle, -10% for unfamiliar foreign bionics (CS, NGR, Poland/Mindwerks), -20% for alien bionics and another -20% for an unknown alien body. A Jury-Rig patch on weapons or bionic systems is at -15% and holds 1D6 days. Any penalty for haste or pressure is halved."
  - name: "Repair and Recalibrate Cybernetics and Bionics"
    description: "Base skill 30%, +5% per level. With time and parts (jury-rigged parts included), fully repairs cybernetics and bionics at 1D6+2 hours per item. A simple implant or simple repair takes 2D4x10 minutes; a complex implant, internal organ or component, or bionic limb 1D4+1 hours. Restores 2D6 M.D.C. per hour to a bionic limb, part or implant, and 2D6+10 per hour to a main body or body armor. Tuning a system (settings, software) gives its owner +5% Speed, +1 P.S. and +1 P.P. for 1D4 weeks."
  - name: "Bionics Acquisition and Reverse Engineering"
    description: "Charged with salvaging bionics from the dead of both sides and watching for enemy depots, convoys and factories, and for new or alien technology to bring home. After 48 hours studying a foreign or alien part, can fit it to a Sovietski cyborg at -30% and make simple repairs to it at -20%, but cannot copy it. The GM may add penalties for very advanced devices."
  - name: "Vedmak Perception and Medical Bonuses"
    description: "+2 on Perception Rolls about cybernetics, bionics, contraband technology, and finding faults in cybernetic and bionic systems and in injuries and illness; +5% to diagnosing physical injury, to surgery and to repairing cybernetics and bionics. The save vs Horror Factor covers the worst battlefield wounds. None of this is raised on the sheet."
  - name: "Mad Doctor"
    description: "At levels 3, 6, 8, 10 and 13 roll percentile (or pick) for a quirk; a repeat is rolled again or grown into a variant with the GM. 01-05 functioning alcoholic; 06-10 functioning drug abuser; 11-15 phobia of a germ or two; 16-20 clean freak off duty; 21-25 hypochondriac under social or combat stress; 26-30 obsessed with getting new and alien bionics, +5% to Cybernetic Medicine and Medical Doctor; 31-35 fascinated by alien bionics, foreign and alien penalties halved; 36-40 god complex, +5% to Cybernetic Medicine, the O.C.C. Skills and other Medical skills, but overconfident; 41-45 studies D-Bees, gains Xenology at +10%; 46-50 fits unwanted bionics to patients and prisoners; 51-55 cybernetics evangelist, +10% to Cybernetic Medicine; 56-60 hates being a cyborg, -5% to Cybernetic Medicine and the Vedmak skills; 61-65 kleptomaniac or bionics hoarder; 66-70 hates bugs, always -1 initiative, -1 strike and -5% to skills, -10% with bugs about; 71-75 cyborg elitist; 76-80 doctor and science elitist; 81-85 paranoid about cyborgs and robots, or the government, Party or enclaves; 86-90 peacemaker; 91-95 trauma migraines lasting 1D6 hours (speed and combat bonuses halved, -1 attack, -30% to skills); 96-00 fear of death, wears home-made 300 M.D.C. armor over the body at -20% to skills, -2 attacks, -2 to all bonuses and half speed. None of these is on the sheet."
  - name: "Vedmak Light Machine Chassis"
    description: "A full conversion light cyborg with six arms; 98% use this chassis, the rest a heavier one of their own (20-30% more M.D.C. to head and main body). M.D.C. by location: head 75 (a human face; a field helmet adds 35), crane arms (2) 120 each, robot arms (2) 60 each, human-looking arms (2) 50 each, retractable utility tool arms (8 or more) 11 each, hands (2) 20 each, feet (2) 25 each, legs (2) 85 each, main body 165 (the mdc_base). Wears no extra armor. Speed 58 (40 mph) at most, being top heavy; legs P.S. and P.P. 20. Each leg has a concealed compartment and one feature of choice (or another compartment); the feet have anchoring spikes."
  - name: "Crane Arms"
    description: "Two large back-mounted arms, Robotic P.S. 40 and P.P. 18, reaching 8 ft (2.4 m) forward and 10 ft (3 m) up, with clamp claws that turn 360 degrees. Each carries a low-profile heavy laser cutter (1D6 or 2D6 M.D., 12 ft/3.7 m, on the nuclear supply), six Cyber-Nano Robot Repair Systems (sovietski-cyber-nano-robot-repair-system) and a concealed compartment. Together they work as Jaws of Life: 2D6+4 M.D. prying, spreading and tearing (they cannot punch), yet gentle enough to lift the wounded. Being top heavy: -10% to balance and leaps at half height and distance."
  - name: "Robot Arms"
    description: "Two arms under the shoulder blades reaching past the human arms, Robotic P.S. 18 and P.P. 18. Left: a laser torch with a second medical scanner, 40 ft (12.2 m), settings 1D6, 2D6, 4D6 and 1D4x10 S.D.C., 1 M.D. and 1D4 M.D., each blast one attack, unlimited payload off the body''s power, detachable as a handheld tool; a light and magnifying glass. Right: a dual system cutter on a folding 3 ft (0.9 m) arm (P.S. 15, P.P. 10); a defibrillator with a medical scanner and Bio-Scan and Bio-Lab, an enhanced portable-bio-scan-bio-lab. Each has a folding utility arm and hand (P.S. 10, P.P. 10)."
  - name: "Bionic Arms and Hands"
    description: "Two human-looking arms, Robotic P.S. 20 and P.P. 20. Left: a circular saw on a thin folding arm, 2.5 ft (0.8 m) reach, P.S. 10 and P.P. 10; a compu-drug-dispenser in the wrist or forearm. Each arm: a folding laser scalpel, 12 ft (3.7 m), settings 1, 1D4, 2D4 and 3D4 S.D.C., each blast one attack, a three hour micro-battery recharged from the body in an hour, three spares in a compartment; a mirror and LED light arm and a vibro-scalpel arm, each 2 ft (0.6 m) reach, P.S. 6 and P.P. 10. Hands, 20 M.D.C. each: a Schematics Hand built into a Multi-Tool hand (schematic-sensor-hand), a Medical Sensor Hand (sovietski-medical-sensor-hand), a wrist feature the player picks, three finger weapons, tools or features per hand (vibro-claws or a laser scalpel among them), and one or two more medical features per arm."
  - name: "Other Bionic Systems"
    description: "Head: Psionic Electromagnetic Dampeners, Universal Headjack (universal-headjack-and-ear-implant) and one option of choice. Eyes: one Macro-Eye Laser (macro-eye-laser) and a Modular Eye socket holding three eyes of choice. Ears: a Sound Identifier set for mechanical faults and an Ultra-Ear for medical ones. Mouth and throat: Molecular Analyzer and Built-In Loudspeaker (sovietski-built-in-loudspeaker). Chest: Oxygen Storage Cell (sovietski-oxygen-storage-cell), Hardened Circuits (sovietski-hardened-circuits) and one feature of choice. The leg and crane arm compartments hold the backup tools and nano-robot systems in the starting equipment; those posted to heavy combat zones carry twice the nano-robots."
