extraction_notes: "Rifts World Book 36: Sovietski printed 108-115 (cache p108-p115, cache page = printed folio + 0 for printed 38-177), a text layer. Printed 109 is a full-page illustration with no text. Printed 111, 112 and 113 were checked against renders, among them the skill list, the M.D.C. by Location block and every arm and tool figure. Heading Vedmak O.C.C., Light Machine Cyber-Doc (printed 108); stats Sovietski Vedmak Cyber-Doc O.C.C. Stats (printed 111), ending on printed 115 above the Spetsnaz Intel O.C.C. A Red Army officer and full conversion cyborg beside the other Sovietski military O.C.C.s, so occ_group men-of-arms and men_of_arms true, as the Warlord Cyber-Doc. || XP: the ladder headed Vedmak Cyber-Doc in the Experience Tables (printed 224, cache p220); its figures match the Cyborg Soldier Heavy Machine ladder. || BODY: the Vedmak Light Machine chassis is the class''s own and has no vessel row, so its main body (165) is mdc_base and the rest of the M.D.C. by Location, the arms, tools and the built-in bionics are prose, citing catalog slugs where a row exists. No row was found for Psionic Electromagnetic Dampeners, the Modular Eye socket, Sound Identifier, Ultra-Ear or a plain Molecular Analyzer. Speed 58 and leg P.S. and P.P. 20 are chassis figures, not stored as attributes. || BONUSES: +1 I.Q., +1 M.A., +3 save vs poison and +3 vs drugs (toxins_poisons and harmful_drugs), +5 vs disease, +3 vs Horror Factor stored. The Perception and +5% medical bonuses are prose. || SKILLS: Computer Operation and Computer Programming print (20%) with no plus sign, read as +20% (checked on the render). W.P. Knife/Scalpel is the catalog''s W.P. Knife. Hovercraft (ground) is Hover Craft (ground). Sensory Equipment is stored at +5% with the medical +20% in its note. Hand to Hand: Basic cannot be changed, so costs is empty. || RELATED: five, at least two from Mechanical or Science (a minimums union), plus one at each of levels 3, 7, 11 and 15. Rogue lists Pick Locks, which the catalog files under Espionage, so an Espionage entry offers Pick Locks only at the Rogue +5%; Find Contraband is a Military row, offered by both lists. Pilot excepts Tanks and APCs, and Robots and Power Armor with every Robot Combat row, Air Assault Armor and Flight System Combat. || SECONDARY: one each at levels 2, 5, 8, 10, 12 and 15, none at level 1. || MAD DOCTOR: the table on printed 110-111 is summarised in the ability; no table rows are stored (the Sovietski plan''s tables ruling). || MONEY: savings of 2D4x1,000 credits stored; the salary is in restrictions. || EQUIPMENT: the medical and surgical kits are their catalog rows with contents in notes; the IRMSS and RMK counts add the body''s nano-robots to the surgical kit''s; the six of each other nano-robot system is stored as six of each row. Not stored as rows: listed in restrictions."
---

## Lore

The Red Army leans on cybernetics more than almost any other force, so it
needs Cyber-Docs in numbers, and it picks the best of them to become Vedmak.
The word is old Slavic, roughly a male witch, though women serve too; it
comes from the way these doctors seem to work sorcery on a broken cyborg,
stripping a Heavy Machine and rebuilding it in hours, in a hospital or under
fire.

A Vedmak is meant to be a one-person triage unit who sends wounded soldiers
and cyborgs back to the line. To do that the doctor gives up a human body for
a full conversion Light Machine frame, keeping only the face if desired. A
pair of crane arms on the back holds heavy frames and peels away armor, a
smaller pair below the shoulders cuts, lights and scans, and the two human
arms are packed with fine tools for surgery and repair. Vedmak also salvage
and gather bionics, keeping the Red Army''s cyborg legions running whatever
the battlefield throws at them.

## GM Notes

On assignment: medivac vehicles, the SU-90 Iron Forge Mobile Cyber-hospital
and other transport, extra weapons, ammunition, medical supplies and
nano-bots, medical assistants, hospitals and their laboratories and operating
rooms, computers, a military escort, rations and field gear. The Vedmak
usually has priority for medical supplies, facilities and equipment, though
availability still depends on the commander, stock, location, casualties and
combat conditions.

A Mad Doctor quirk is rolled at levels 3, 6, 8, 10 and 13; the GM may add
other quirks or insanities from Rifts Ultimate Edition, short of anything too
crippling for a player character.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sovietski-vedmak-cyber-doc');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sovietski-vedmak-cyber-doc';

